---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Haley Parks"
  description="How Haley Parks approaches product strategy, research, systems, and the work of making complex things useful."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "About" }]}
>
  <article class="maria-page maria-prose">
    <header class="maria-collection-head">
      <p class="maria-eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>I make complex systems easier to understand and use.</h1>
      <p>
        My work sits between product strategy, research, operations, and the
        careful translation required to turn ambiguity into something people can
        act on.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="maria-split">
      <h2>How I think</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          I am drawn to problems that are difficult for more than one reason:
          the information is incomplete, the system has many owners, and the
          people inside it do not share the same mental model.
        </p>
        <p>
          My contribution is usually a combination of listening, structuring,
          and making. I look for the decisions hidden inside the noise, create a
          useful model of the situation, and build the smallest credible thing
          that helps a team move.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <blockquote class="maria-statement">
      <p>
        Good systems should make people feel more capable, not more managed.
      </p>
      <footer>A working belief</footer>
    </blockquote>

    <section class="maria-split">
      <h2>What shapes the work</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          I have worked across complex service environments where strategy,
          delivery, policy, data, and frontline experience all meet. That work
          taught me to treat operating reality as part of the product.
        </p>
        <p>
          Writing is how I test ideas, preserve useful context, and notice
          connections between domains. The site keeps polished essays, project
          evidence, and smaller observations distinct without pretending they
          are unrelated.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="maria-split maria-principles">
      <h2>What I try to bring to the room</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Clarity without false certainty.</strong> Name what is known, assumed,
          and still to learn.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Respect for lived expertise.</strong> The people closest to a system
          often understand its real constraints best.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Evidence that travels.</strong> Research matters when it can survive
          the meeting where the researcher is absent.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Care in the details.</strong> Small choices accumulate into trust,
          friction, and experience quality.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="maria-contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="maria-eyebrow">Contact</p>
        <h2 id="contact-heading">
          A useful conversation is a good place to start.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          If you are working through a complicated product or organizational
          question, I am always interested in comparing notes.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:hello@haleyparks.com">Email</a> · <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/haleyparks/"
            rel="me">LinkedIn</a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
